TITLE:: RLRecall
summary:: What a line has done so far: after the same last values, what it did next
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLLine, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
A memory of one line, kept as it goes: after the same last values (its last steps), what it did next. Orders 0 (how often each value came) to link::#-depth::, each leaning on the one below; with nothing seen, every value alike.

A figure that comes back in a line is one it has already said. link::Classes/RLLine:: draws with an RLRecall of the steps it has drawn, so that a line takes up its own motives, on any pitch. Measured on solos (HomewareSC, code::Math/Category_Theory/fit/jazz_know.py::), this memory of the solo itself saves a tenth of a bit a note over what solos do in general, and lines drawn with it come back to their own figures as often as the players' do (six in ten of a line's three-step figures are different, against eight in ten without it).

code::
~r = RLRecall(49);                 // 49 values: steps of -24 to 24 semitones, 24 the same pitch
~r.learn([], 26);                  // a tone up
~r.learn([26], 26);                // after a tone up, a tone up
~r.learn([26, 26], 21);            // after two, a minor third down
~r.chances([26, 26]).maxIndex;     // 21: the likeliest again
~r.chances([26]).maxIndex;         // 26
~r.chances([30, 26]).maxIndex;     // 26: a longer memory that never came leans on the shorter one
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: size
How many values there are.
argument:: depth
How many last values it looks at, at the most.
argument:: lean
How much each order leans on the one below, in notes: with 1, a figure said twice is nearly a rule.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: chances
The chances of each value after these last values (the most recent last).

METHOD:: learn
What came after these last values.

METHOD:: size
METHOD:: depth
METHOD:: lean
